/// The hk Pkl package, re-exported as typealiases plus `builtins`. Every other
/// module in the preset reaches hk through this one rather than naming the
/// package, so the preset pins hk once and a new module adds no pin.
///
/// Named `HkPackage` rather than `Hk`: hk looks for its config as `hk.pkl`, and
/// on a case-insensitive filesystem a module named `Hk.pkl` answers to that
/// name.
///
/// A consumer's `hk.pkl` still pins hk a second time, in its `amends`, which
/// takes a literal URI and so cannot read the version from here. hk's own
/// evaluator tolerates the two differing (#392); the Renovate preset groups
/// `hk` with `hk-config` so they move together regardless.
module gtbuchanan.hk.HkPackage

import "package://github.com/jdx/hk/releases/download/v2.13.0/hk@2.13.0#/Config.pkl"
import "package://github.com/jdx/hk/releases/download/v2.13.0/hk@2.13.0#/Builtins.pkl"

typealias Step = Config.Step

typealias Hook = Config.Hook

/// hk runs a step's `Script` per OS, and a plain string through `cmd.exe` on
/// Windows, where a POSIX one-liner fails to parse.
typealias Script = Config.Script

/// A builtin's command alongside its declared `effect`. Amending a builtin's
/// command through this keeps the effect tracking upstream.
typealias CommandSpec = Config.CommandSpec

typealias Command = Config.Command

typealias FileSelector = Config.FileSelector

/// hk's builtin steps. Amend one rather than replacing it, so its declared
/// `effect` and future defaults keep tracking upstream.
builtins = Builtins
